{"title":"2013 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/6/1661ee6ba75b1df39577c967cb0f537cc66e97af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26edbd87f49eb68ec9b662b602db712e5151dc9c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\min(\\sqrt{x+xyz},\\sqrt{y+xyz},\\sqrt{z+xyz})=\\sqrt{x-1}+\\sqrt{y-1}+\\sqrt{z-1}.\\]\" width=\"516\" height=\"22\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28Cauchy_or_AM-GM.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(Cauchy_or_AM-GM)\">Solution  (Cauchy or AM-GM)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution  (Cauchy or AM-GM)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The key Lemma is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89c079faf2cc90b77fda0c975e6cf300099330b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{a-1}+\\sqrt{b-1} \\le \\sqrt{ab}\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec893ca22ac75b59090381fcab8cabf89996e7c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" />. Equality holds when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8e1b67568ce2d5a245ee575c448189947a1a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-1)(b-1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>This is proven easily.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c30a1f27fa074738820cab231ff7889f8ee58be3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{a-1}+\\sqrt{b-1} = \\sqrt{a-1}\\sqrt{1}+\\sqrt{1}\\sqrt{b-1} \\le \\sqrt{(a-1+1)(b-1+1)} = \\sqrt{ab}\\]\" width=\"590\" height=\"32\" /> by Cauchy.\n</p><p>Equality then holds when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb4d2b64ffb3c33a395fb60ef0d5d11d16f0bc8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-1 =\\frac{1}{b-1} \\implies (a-1)(b-1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"298\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Now assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e67141e6f0bb47ae2ae6da6f56c62a6cd495b75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\min(x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />. Now note that, by the Lemma,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/ded115d5095ab51514d54b6018fd74e04843a475.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{x-1}+\\sqrt{y-1}+\\sqrt{z-1} \\le \\sqrt{x-1} + \\sqrt{yz} \\le \\sqrt{x(yz+1)} = \\sqrt{xyz+x}\\]\" width=\"545\" height=\"32\" />. So equality must hold in order for the condition in the problem statement to be met.\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54cd379fb18797783e3f316d5428d28f6d4319cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y-1)(z-1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/d/5ad4f0507234c58d600fd7a6b7d8c8a17111ba11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)(yz) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />. If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f00b55e82a7f1feb0c3854e8e54adea4b52bcaa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = c$\" width=\"41\" height=\"8\" />, then we can easily compute that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/165993d6d9c0c3d27e87ac508ab90ce868f2e51d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{c}{c-1}, x = \\frac{c^2+c-1}{c^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"198\" height=\"39\" />.\nNow it remains to check that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8ab8c41a044bd5b8314b4e42c5b1202a013d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>But by easy computations, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cd58ab3a0fb46579cf238211659e9b8f8c614ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{c^2+c-1}{c^2} \\le c = z \\Longleftrightarrow (c^2-1)(c-1) \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"371\" height=\"39\" />, which is obvious.\nAlso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cba13cb96e8c351ae3307ea1d207f176785206b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{c^2+c-1}{c^2} \\le \\frac{c}{c-1} = y \\Longleftrightarrow 2c \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"309\" height=\"39\" />, which is obvious, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66fc9dbd593f92b7f0a52a17fc98b275c19671e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>So all solutions are of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8ab1b66d4f6a0281566f294aab74aed0d09a83c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\left(\\frac{c^2+c-1}{c^2}, \\frac{c}{c-1}, c\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"187\" height=\"56\" />, and all permutations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/2/2c24e4f8b8d4c523fd3bf262b8b50766c19777b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><b>Remark:</b> An alternative proof of the key Lemma is the following:\nBy AM-GM, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/5/525af74927e6fab47f032d8532898bebb4ff87ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(ab-a-b+1)+1 = (a-1)(b-1) + 1 \\ge 2\\sqrt{(a-1)(b-1)}\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/610f5957ee1a815e06e5965507e02456ff1ac6d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ab\\ge (a-1)+(b-1)+2\\sqrt{(a-1)(b-1)}\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"32\" />. Now taking the square root of both sides gives the desired. Equality holds when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7f7b0aea7ef9a93d32c7813f732c4ac254be32d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-1)(b-1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG,  assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e67141e6f0bb47ae2ae6da6f56c62a6cd495b75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\min(x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e0d58274300be6fd20febc2397cab19140ef869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\sqrt{x-1},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"19\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fcf6611997663298179b9b89ce9b08b72c2189c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\sqrt{y-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/7/9d7110cdb3f82f686678a59309a063e1b55888e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\sqrt{z-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a1be21b231ec76a75a9d0341fedf29f8e82e732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da78d1674d72d683ca93644875f1d0ed718efb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=b^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/8742b6bb7f4f6039d949b65c0845bb84dd92cc03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=c^2+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />. The equation becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d43c054d5dcc9444d4d9cb314b5889cf4746bf3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a^2+1)+(a^2+1)(b^2+1)(c^2+1)=(a+b+c)^2.\\]\" width=\"386\" height=\"19\" />\nRearranging the terms, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2666df29733bc1db9b528398a06fe00675ffdd84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1+a^2)(bc-1)^2+[a(b+c)-1]^2=0.\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"20\" />\nTherefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfa836da5bc99e5969c48c2bcae7a8704c20d9c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bc=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c680f02ec354643b791d0e963386f0c84f7a616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(b+c)=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> Express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/6/7b60df039e1229e00e8a5c43289de8230a431bea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{c}{c^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"83\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a4df4396ae585ab9248bdfaae7061f507650e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{1}{c}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"48\" height=\"37\" /> Easy to check that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the smallest among <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/201a2eef545643b50b07fed5c09e894bcced5c58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c.$\" width=\"11\" height=\"8\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/7/f174ce78eb79bbc4285c4111bce7c2a67d755f2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{c^4+3c^2+1}{(c^2+1)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"130\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/a/a5a3185b34646470440deda5b2d813b559e1cab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{c^2+1}{c^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff6fdf8452fc8c3253f040683886f146d32869c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=c^2+1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4ca627dfef0d03355984158ba53e518a40147a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2=t$\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, we have the solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73ed093cc73a8d9a14185fa525e7067e5c3725d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca76a9d75f72faea42a980b88de56ea08516b6e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{t^2+3t+1}{(t+1)^2}, \\frac{t+1}{t}, t+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"195\" height=\"43\" /> and permutations for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b04f674320a5061a0473ea63f1a6195d731703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t&gt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> \n</p><p>--J.Z.\n</p>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017233143\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 205/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 335/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9229/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.188      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n100.00%    5.188      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11945:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017233143 and revision id 230738. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}